{
  "about": "Typological claims taken from published reference works rather than written from memory. Each claim is recorded as that source gives it, with its own references, and is then checked and measured by tools/typology-sources.mjs. Recording a claim is not endorsing it.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "torrey",
      "citation": "R. A. Torrey, The New Topical Text Book (1897), article 'Types of Christ'. Public domain.",
      "retrieved": "https://www.studylight.org/concordances/ttt/t/types-of-christ.html",
      "note": "Transcribed as given. Two transcription corrections are recorded in the claims themselves: the entry printed 'Man' is 'Manna' (its references are Exodus 16:11-15 and John 6:32-35), and 'Vail' is the veil of the tabernacle. Torrey's references follow the King James versification; where that differs from the ASV the tool reports it rather than silently adjusting."
    },
    {
      "id": "pink",
      "citation": "A. W. Pink, The Antichrist (1923), chapter 13, 'Types of the Antichrist'. Public domain.",
      "retrieved": "https://www.ccel.org/ccel/pink/antichrist.chap13.html",
      "note": "Ten characters are profiled in detail; six more are named in passing. Both are transcribed, marked by how the chapter treats them."
    },
    {
      "id": "yetter",
      "citation": "A. H. Yetter, 'The Anti-Christ in the Types', Grace and Truth Magazine.",
      "retrieved": "https://www.swartzentrover.com/cotor/bible/Doctrines/LastThings/The%20Anti-Christ%20in%20the%20Types.htm",
      "note": "Four types with detailed reference runs. One printed reference, Daniel 1:24-27, does not exist; the passage described is Daniel 3:24-27, and it is recorded here as printed with the discrepancy noted rather than silently corrected."
    }
  ],
